  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying 'probable' outcomes (those above 50% probability) and averaging them. However, the individual did not categorize outcomes based on a 50% threshold or exclude outcomes below that threshold. Instead, they explicitly weighed both the 33% and 34% probabilities as relevant and compared them directly. They also focused on the monetary difference and subjectively evaluated the trade-off, which is inconsistent with the mechanical rule of averaging only 'probable' outcomes. Furthermore, both lotteries have only 0 as a 'probable' outcome under the reason’s definition, so the reason would imply indifference, whereas the individual actively preferred B based on a different rationale. There is no evidence that the individual applied a 50% threshold to filter outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
